Now let me verify behavior preservation by comparing base vs head versions of mergeBot.js function by function. Key areas to scrutinize:

1. `resolveRepoTarget(job)` — original: `job.repo` — note the original code does `var job = (params && params.jobParams) || {}; var repo = job.repo;`. New: `resolveRepoTarget(job)` with `var repo = job.repo;`. Same.

2. `rollupDetail` — the diff shows the old code had:
```
if (!runs.length) {
   ...workflow fallback...
   return { state: 'none', pendingSince: null };
}
if (!runs.length) return { state: 'none', pendingSince: null };
```
The second `if (!runs.length)` is dead code (redundant guard kept verbatim, as PR notes). Fine.

3. `fetchCheckRuns` — original:
```
var cr = parseMcp(github_get_commit_check_runs({...}));
var runs = ... // something parsing check_runs
```
Let me check the full current file and base file to verify the extraction didn't lose anything, e.g. how `runs` is derived from `cr`.

4. `hasActiveSmRun` — original used `runs = []` then try/catch with fallback; catch returns false. New: `listSmRuns` returns null on catch; `runs === null → false`. Same semantics? Original: in the catch, return false. New: listSmRuns catches and returns null; hasActiveSmRun returns false. Same. But note: original `runs` starts as `[]` and if try succeeds, runs may be empty → loop doesn't run → return false. Same.

One subtle behavior difference in `hasActiveSmRun`: original iterated `runs[i]` with `var r = runs[i] || {}`. New: `isLiveSmRun(runs[i] || {}, now)`. Same.

Another subtlety: `isLiveSmRun` in the original: `if (s !== 'queued' && ...) continue;` — new returns false. Same.

Zombie check: original: `var ts = Date.parse(r.updated_at || r.updatedAt || r.created_at || r.createdAt || ''); if (!isNaN(ts) && (now - ts) > 6*60*60*100) continue;` New `isZombieSmRun` returns `!isNaN(ts) && (now - ts) > 6*60*60*100`, and isLiveSmRun: `if (s !== 'in_progress' && isZombieSmRun(r, now)) return false;`. Same.

5. In `action()`, the advanced-merge path:
Original:
```
if (approved && labels.indexOf('agent:review') === -1) {
   var advance = deadHeadPassed && labels.indexOf('ai_validated') !== -1;
   if (advance) deadHeadPassed = false; // consumed by the first live candidate
   var advanced = false;
   if (advance) {
       var upRollup = checksRollup(...);
       if (upRollup === 'green' && mergeStateOf(pr) === 'CLEAN') {
           var um = squashMerge(...);
           if (um.merged) { say(...); acted++; advanced = true; }
           else { say('❌ ... merge refused: ' + um.error); }
       }
   }
   if (!advanced) { ... FIFO-queued line ... }
   continue;
}
```
New:
```
if (approved && !hasLabel(labels, 'agent:review')) {
   var advanced = false;
   if (deadHeadPassed && hasLabel(labels, 'ai_validated')) {
       deadHeadPassed = false;
       var upRollup = checksRollup(...);
       if (upRollup === 'green' && mergeStateOf(pr) === 'CLEAN') {
           var gained = mergeApprovedHead(owner, name, pr, '🧲 ...', say);
           if (gained) { acted += gained; advanced = true; }
       }
   }
   if (!advanced) { ... }
   continue;
}
```

Difference: In the original, `deadHeadPassed = false` was consumed when `advance` is true — i.e., when deadHeadPassed && has ai_validated. In the new code, `deadHeadPassed = false` is set inside the `if (deadHeadPassed && hasLabel(labels, 'ai_validated'))` block — same condition. So equivalent. BUT: subtle difference — in the original, `deadHeadPassed = false` happens even if the rollup isn't green / merge refused. New code: same — deadHeadPassed = false is set when entering the advance block, before rollup. Equivalent.

But wait — there's a subtle difference in the new code: `if (gained) { acted += gained; advanced = true; }` — mergeApprovedHead returns 1 on success, 0 on refusal and logs refusal. Equivalent to original.

Another subtlety: in `unarmStaleHead`, the original logged `stillHours` computed from `Date.now() - detail.pendingSince`. New computes `Math.round(((Date.now() - pendingSince) / 360000) * 10) / 10` — same.

